### Install the "REST Client" extension in VS Code, then click "Send Request" above each request.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Get all events (default page 1, limit 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events

### 2. Filter by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?category=technology

### 3. Filter by publication status
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?isPublished=true

### 4. Sort and paginate
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?sortBy=eventDate&order=asc&page=2&limit=2

### 5. Upcoming events
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/upcoming

### 6. Existing event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101

### 7. Missing event -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/not-real

### 8. Sessions of an event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101/sessions

### 9. One session under its event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101/sessions/ses-201

### 9b. Session that belongs to a DIFFERENT event -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/evt-101/sessions/ses-204

### 10. Create a valid event -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Intro to Cloud Computing",
  "description": "A beginner-friendly campus workshop.",
  "location": "Engineering Block, Room 2",
  "eventDate": "2026-12-04T09:00:00.000Z",
  "category": "technology",
  "isPublished": true
}

### 11. Create an event with a missing title -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "No title here.",
  "location": "Main Hall",
  "eventDate": "2026-12-04T09:00:00.000Z",
  "category": "technology"
}

### Extra: invalid sort field -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?sortBy=price

### Extra: invalid page -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?page=abc

### Extra (stretch): search, date range, location, published
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?search=hack
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?dateFrom=2026-12-01&dateTo=2026-12-31
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?location=main
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/published
